      "description": "MIM & MIF Program Coordinator (Temporary) - IESE Business School This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. IESE Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, that is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Skip to main content Career menu Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage iese.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Madrid, Spain · Hybrid MIM & MIF Program Coordinator (Temporary) Coordinate IESE's MIM & MIF programs to deliver seamless, high-quality participant experiences through cross-functional collaboration and continuous improvement. Apply for this job The MIM & MIF Program Coordinator is responsible for the operational planning, coordination, and execution of the Master in Management (MIM) and Master in Finance (MIF) programs, ensuring an outstanding participant experience and the smooth delivery of all program activities. Working closely with faculty, students, internal departments, and external partners, the Coordinator plays a key role in guaranteeing operational excellence while continuously improving processes and services. We are looking for a temporary employee who can work with us for a 3 Month contract . Key Responsibilities Coordinate the day-to-day operations of the MIM and MIF programs from participant onboarding through graduation. Ensure the successful execution of academic activities, including class logistics, examinations, program events, and international modules where applicable. Serve as a primary point of contact for participants, providing timely support and guidance throughout their academic journey. Coordinate with faculty and academic departments to ensure the smooth delivery of courses and learning activities. Collaborate with Admissions, Career Development, Student Affairs, International Office, Operations, IT, Finance, and other internal teams to ensure a seamless student experience. Monitor program calendars, deadlines, communications, and administrative processes, ensuring accuracy and timely execution. Maintain program documentation and student records in institutional systems, ensuring data quality and compliance with internal policies. Identify opportunities to improve operational processes, participant experience, and cross-functional collaboration. Support the preparation of reports, surveys, and program performance metrics to facilitate continuous improvement. Contribute to special projects and initiatives related to program innovation and operational excellence. Requirements Bachelor's degree. Previous experience in program coordination, project management, higher education, customer service, or a similar role. Excellent organizational and planning skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously. Strong service orientation and commitment to delivering an exceptional participant experience. Ability to work effectively with multiple stakeholders in a collaborative and international environment. High attention to detail and strong problem-solving capabilities. Excellent communication skills in English and Spanish, both written and spoken. Strong digital skills and experience using information systems and Microsoft Office applications. Proactive mindset with a continuous improvement orientation and the ability to work autonomously. Locations Madrid, Spain Remote status Hybrid Apply for this job Madrid, Spain · Hybrid MIM & MIF Program Coordinator (Temporary) Coordinate IESE's MIM & MIF programs to deliver seamless, high-quality participant experiences through cross-functional collaboration and continuous improvement. Loading application form Close modal Career site Data & privacy Manage cookies iese.edu/ LinkedIn Instagram Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at IESE Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
